<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Austral Islands</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tubuai Islands</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Austral Islands are the southernmost island group of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a> in the South Pacific, including Rurutu, Tubuai, Rimatara, Raivavae and Rapa. Their chiefs came under Tahitian influence in the 19th century, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed the islands one by one between 1880 and 1901. Their small population lives mainly from farming and fishing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austral-islands.jpg" alt="Austral Islands" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guilherme Paula · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Austral_Islands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
